mediatek: ubispl: don't NOTICE-spam on empty (erased) UBI blocks

The raw-UBI BL2 scan prints "Bad EC magic in block N ffffffff" via NOTICE for
every erased/empty block (EC magic 0xffffffff). On our boards the SPI-NAND tail
is full of empty blocks, so the serial console is flooded at every NAND boot. An
empty (never-written) block is normal, not an error -> demote it to VERBOSE
(ubi_dbg). A genuinely corrupt magic still prints NOTICE.

Affects every board's spim-nand BL2 (the ATF package is shared); log-only change,
boot behaviour is unchanged.
--- a/drivers/io/ubi/ubispl.c
+++ b/drivers/io/ubi/ubispl.c
@@ -244,7 +244,10 @@
 	/* Magic number available ? */
 	magic = be32toh(eh.magic);
 	if (magic != UBI_EC_HDR_MAGIC) {
-		ubi_msg("Bad EC magic in block %d %08x", pnum, magic);
+		if (magic == 0xffffffff)
+			ubi_dbg("Empty (erased) block %d", pnum);
+		else
+			ubi_msg("Bad EC magic in block %d %08x", pnum, magic);
 		goto out;
 	}
 
